<title>UK: Navia/E+H post offer for Whessoe.</title>
<headline>Navia/E+H post offer for Whessoe.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway's Navia ASA and its Swiss partner Endress+Hauser said on Friday that they had posted the document for their joint recommended cash offer for British instrument and controls group Whessoe Plc on Thursday.</p>
<p>&quot;Acceptances should be received by 1500 GMT on March 27,&quot; the companies said in a statement.</p>
<p>Norwegian technology company Navia, which also specialises in instrumentation, has been buying stock with E+H at their offer price of 175p, and said earlier this week they held about 51 percent of Whessoe.</p>
<p>--London newsroom +44-171 542 7717</p>
</text>
